WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.365
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Thursday, November fifth.

2
00:00:04.365 --> 00:00:11.928
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:11.928 --> 00:00:14.395
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.395 --> 00:00:32.051
Today: a new wave of bomb threats against flights in Europe, the rising death toll from a Russian strike on an aid distribution point in Ukraine, a nationwide strike in France, a security operation against protesters in Pakistan administered Kashmir, and new U.S. sanctions on Iran's weapons and shipping networks.

5
00:00:32.051 --> 00:00:35.431
We start with an update on Europe's aviation bomb threats.

6
00:00:35.431 --> 00:00:46.811
Reuters reports a bomb alert diverted an Airbus A320 flying from Dublin to Rome, according to the French prime minister, and a Finnair flight landed in Rome after a separate bomb alert this morning.

7
00:00:46.811 --> 00:00:53.427
The terrorism tracker TRAC says the new wave targeted at least twelve passenger flights across Europe.

8
00:00:53.427 --> 00:00:54.162
Turning to Ukraine.

9
00:00:54.162 --> 00:01:06.098
Reuters reports the death toll from a Russian bombing of an aid distribution point in the Zaporizhzhia region on Monday, November second, has risen to thirty seven, with dozens still missing, officials said.

10
00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:07.109
Next, France.

11
00:01:07.109 --> 00:01:07.938
The U.S.

12
00:01:07.938 --> 00:01:19.366
State Department says a nationwide multi sector strike is planned for today, affecting teachers, healthcare workers, government employees and public transport, with the four largest railway unions calling a joint national strike.

13
00:01:19.366 --> 00:01:33.948
It says recent demonstrations were violent and involved property destruction and looting, that local curfews in parts of France, including some Paris neighborhoods, could continue, and it advises avoiding demonstrations and large gatherings.

14
00:01:33.948 --> 00:01:34.868
In Pakistan.

15
00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:46.642
Hum News reports security forces said they cleared a bus terminal in Rawalakot, in Azad Jammu and Kashmir, this morning, after an early morning operation against protesters who had occupied the area for about five months.

16
00:01:46.642 --> 00:01:54.373
Police in Poonch said they were removing illegal barricades, and police and protesters both reported injuries after an exchange of fire.

17
00:01:54.373 --> 00:02:00.975
The protest movement, the Joint Awami Action Committee, says three protesters were killed and twenty one injured.

18
00:02:00.975 --> 00:02:02.345
And on sanctions.

19
00:02:02.345 --> 00:02:03.301
The U.S.

20
00:02:03.301 --> 00:02:18.861
Treasury says it targeted an India based network that provided false flags and certifications to sanctioned vessels carrying Iranian petroleum, and the State Department says the action covers thirteen individuals and companies, plus a Turkey based firm servicing sanctioned Iranian airlines.

21
00:02:18.861 --> 00:02:27.383
Separately, the State Department says it sanctioned two individuals and one entity involved in Iran's efforts to acquire shoulder fired air defense missiles.

22
00:02:27.383 --> 00:02:30.635
Now a few quick notes by region.

23
00:02:30.635 --> 00:02:42.180
In Africa, Critical Threats says the Rapid Support Forces and an allied militia captured the town of Sali, about eighty miles south of the Blue Nile state capital Ad Damazin in Sudan, on Tuesday, November third.

24
00:02:42.180 --> 00:03:01.546
In the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Radio Okapi reports hundreds of families fled a new attack attributed to the A D F armed group in the Bapere sector of Lubero territory on Tuesday, and Congolese media report twenty nine hostages held by the A D F were freed in joint Congolese and Ugandan army operations in Ituri.

25
00:03:01.546 --> 00:03:15.245
In Europe, the Institute for the Study of War reports Russia's drone strikes on Ukrainian energy infrastructure overnight Tuesday into Wednesday heavily targeted central and western Ukraine and caused significant power outages across the country.

26
00:03:15.245 --> 00:03:22.170
In the Middle East, Reuters reports Turkey's parliament is set to ratify a defense pact with Saudi Arabia and Pakistan as Houthi attacks mount.

27
00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:30.352
In Asia, Reuters reports North Korea says it tested an air defense missile and staged a cruise missile drill.

28
00:03:30.352 --> 00:03:37.159
In health, Reuters reports a British healthcare worker with Ebola is to be evacuated from Congo to the United Kingdom, according to a document it has seen.

29
00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:39.339
The U.K.

30
00:03:39.339 --> 00:03:44.729
Foreign Office updated its Ghana travel advice with information on Ebola screening.

31
00:03:44.729 --> 00:03:54.336
And in cyber, The Record reports a suspected Russian cyberattack disrupted the website of the Kyiv Independent, one of Ukraine's leading English language news outlets.

32
00:03:54.336 --> 00:04:04.407
In an update on the wave of attacks on refrigeration systems across Europe, The Record reports temperature controls were altered at three sites of France's national blood service this week.

33
00:04:04.407 --> 00:04:13.011
It also reports a major Russian web hosting provider is struggling to restore services after a cyberattack destroyed data across its cloud infrastructure.

34
00:04:13.011 --> 00:04:14.451
That's today's brief.

35
00:04:14.451 --> 00:04:22.531
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

36
00:04:22.531 --> 00:04:30.754
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

37
00:04:30.754 --> 00:04:32.900
This brief is digitally narrated.

38
00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:33.854
Questions?

39
00:04:33.854 --> 00:04:37.238
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

40
00:04:37.238 --> 00:04:39.173
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
